EN+=[
 ('second-emilia','The Second Emilia','A Novel','Judith Bahlmann',N,'Forensic evaluator Dr. Emilia von Hardenberg has one task: to assess Alexander Brenner, the former head of a private youth facility, and the methods he learned at a boarding school that officially no longer exists. The deeper she digs, the more the line blurs between professional curiosity and something far more personal. A psychological literary thriller about memory and repression.'),
 ('gardeners','The Gardeners of History','A Novel','Markus Wieland',N,'What if history isn’t only written, but made? A historian, a local journalist, a private investigator and a man who has quietly carried out assignments for twelve years follow four separate traces that all lead to the same place: an inconspicuous company in Frankfurt’s Westend. An atmospheric conspiracy thriller about power, manipulation and who decides what becomes history.'),
 ('beyond-sky','Beyond the Sky','A Novel','Leo Winter',N,'Four teenagers. An old shed. An idea bigger than their world. Over one long winter of Saturdays, Leon and his friends turn a brewery tank from the local junkyard into a spacecraft, and one early summer morning they climb inside. A warm, quietly told coming-of-age novel about curiosity, friendship and the courage to think bigger.'),
 ('theme-park','We’re Going to the Theme Park','A Novel','Tobias Kranz',N,'It was supposed to be an ordinary family day out. Then, over lunch at Fabelland, the tables begin to shake, and something beneath the park is awake. A horror thriller about a family that has forgotten how to talk to one another, and a single day that forces them to stay together or lose everything.'),
 ('addiction','Addiction','A Novel','Sandro Urban',N,'Marcel breaks into other people’s houses to pay for what he can no longer live without. Then one afternoon a homeowner comes home early, finds him on her stairs and does not scream. A quiet, unflinching novel about addiction, guilt and trust, about relapse and honesty, and about what it takes to get up again the next morning.'),
 ('colombia','The Hidden Side of Colombia','30 Places Off the Beaten Track','Mika Solberg',F,'Cartels or Caribbean beaches: this guide takes you to a third Colombia, the quiet, generous one. 30 places off the beaten track, from Mompox and the cloud forest of Minca to Caño Cristales and the whales of Nuquí, each with a practical toolkit, plus honest budgets, safety notes and itineraries of 7 to 30 days.'),
 ('peru','The Hidden Side of Peru','30 Places Off the Beaten Track','Mika Solberg',F,'Tell people you’re going to Peru, and they say: Machu Picchu, right? This guide is about everything else: 30 places off the beaten track, from Kuélap and Gocta to the Cordillera Blanca, Choquequirao and the Cotahuasi Canyon, with a practical toolkit for each, realistic budgets, altitude advice and itineraries.'),
 ('grown-up','Playing Grown-Up','Why the Child in Us Stays – and What It Really Means to Grow Up','Friedhelm Westerkamp',F,'You’re not too sensitive. You’re reacting the way you once learned to. Drawing on attachment research and developmental psychology, this book explains in plain language why old experiences still steer present-day reactions, and how to live with the child in us: to feel without being ruled, to set boundaries without guilt and to keep our curiosity.'),
 ('gen-algorithm','Generation Algorithm','How Algorithms, TikTok, and Social Media Are Changing the Way We Think','Friedhelm Westerkamp',F,'You think you decide what you see. Most of the time, the algorithm has already decided. From infinite scroll to an economy that treats attention as a raw material: a clear, balanced and well-sourced book about how the feed shapes our thinking, with concrete steps for parents, young people, schools and policymakers.'),
 ('piercing','The Piercing Academy','Your Path to Becoming a Body Piercer','Alessandro Noto',F,'A practical textbook for aspiring body piercers: legal basics and consent, history, pain and local anesthetics, hygiene and sterile technique, aftercare, materials, jewelry and tools, and an overview of ear, face, body and genital piercings, closing with the procedure step by step. Contains photographs of genital piercings. For readers aged 18 and over.'),
 ('delegation','The Delegation System','How to Finally Let Go as a Mom, Without Having to Do Everything Yourself','Alessandro Noto',F,'You’re not overwhelmed because you can’t do it. You’re overwhelmed because you’re carrying too much. A short, practical workbook for exhausted moms: what the mental load really is, the 5 traps almost every mom falls into, a clear 4-step plan, a Family Board template and a conversation guide for your partner.'),
 ('soccer','The Dark Side of Soccer','Scandals. Power. Money.','Jan Völker',F,'Everyone knows soccer. Hardly anyone knows what happens behind the opening whistle. Twenty-five true stories from seven decades of the world’s most popular sport, from the 1971 Bundesliga bribery scandal and Hillsborough to FIFA arrests and the 2022 World Cup in Qatar, each with a fact box and source notes.'),
 ('power-woman','Project Power Woman','Transforming Body, Mind, and Self-Confidence','Victor Cross',F,'Most women don’t lose themselves in one dramatic crisis, but one reasonable sacrifice at a time. A direct, practical system for getting back: strength training, nutrition and energy, sleep, cycle and hormones, charisma and self-confidence, focus and routines, closing with the Power Woman Code and a 30-day challenge.'),
 ('superhuman','Project Superhuman','Transforming Body, Mind, and Identity','Victor Cross',F,'Most men don’t grow weak overnight, but in small, reasonable steps. A direct, no-nonsense guide in five parts: mindset and discipline, training and recovery, nutrition, presence and self-confidence, focus, routines and mission, with training plans, a 7-day nutrition plan, a 30-day challenge and a 90-day roadmap.'),
]
